          "q": "Can a Connecticut skunk be taken away and released in the woods?",
          "a": "No. Skunks are a rabies-vector species in Connecticut and moving one off the property is prohibited by statute. That is why we recommend a licensed NWCO: the handling on site, the den sealing, and the barrier work are what actually end the problem."
