          "a": "Usually not by itself. Grubs are part of a mole's diet, but earthworms are the staple, and a moist, well-kept Connecticut lawn stays attractive after grub treatment. Trapping the active travel tunnels is what ends the ridging; we probe and mark tunnels to find them."
