          "a": "Pigeons, European starlings, and house sparrows are the birds we remove and exclude as routine Delaware work, under our company permit. Canada geese and woodpeckers are protected under the Migratory Bird Treaty Act, so goose nest or egg work and woodpecker work require federal and state authorization; our role there is deterrence, timing, and referral, and we will say so on the first call rather than sell a removal we cannot lawfully do."
