          "q": "Why are squirrels getting into my Rhode Island triple-decker?",
          "a": "Because a triple-decker offers three floors of soffits, dormers, and porch-roof junctions, and street trees in Providence and Pawtucket bridge straight onto them. A thorough job maps and seals every floor's entries, not just the one at the top — otherwise the squirrels simply move down a storey."
