          "q": "What are the Rhode Island rules for groundhog removal?",
          "a": "The woodchuck is both an NWCS-authorized species in Rhode Island and, by definition in DEM's rules, a rabies-vector species — in the same list as raccoon, skunk, bat, and fox. Rhode Island also bars moving a live-caught mammal off the property, so our woodchuck work is trapping at the burrow, confirmation that the system is empty, and closure with barrier protection, all on the property where the animal was caught."
