          "q": "An opossum is living in my Rhode Island basement. How did it get in?",
          "a": "Most often through a rotted bulkhead, a broken basement window, or a foundation gap at ground level — opossums are poor climbers for a house entry but excellent at finding a ground-level door left ajar by age. We remove the animal, clean the den area, and seal the entry, which in an older Rhode Island home usually means the bulkhead."
